# Three local folders, never committed. Each manages a different unique circumstance;
# see the README's "Local folders" section for which is which.
# Both spellings of memory are ignored so a folder created under either name cannot leak.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash: these ignore the real folders at the repository root and
# NOT the copies under templates/layout/, which exist precisely to be committed and handed
# to an adopter. Unanchored, git matches the name at any depth and silently swallows the
# templates -- which it did, until this was caught.
/.memory/
/memory/
*.memory.md
/.profile/
/.workgroup/

# A global gitignore on this machine also ignores `.memory/` at any depth, and a repo rule
# is read after it, so the templates are re-included explicitly. The directory must be
# un-ignored before its contents can be: git will not look inside an excluded directory.
!templates/layout/.memory/
!templates/layout/.memory/**
!templates/layout/.profile/
!templates/layout/.profile/**
!templates/layout/.workgroup/
!templates/layout/.workgroup/**
